From 208c24d24e8631cc0a79aa6408832a6e17153da2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment archive <experiment@invalid.example>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:02:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wlan: capture native adapter-stop decisions

Retain the evaluated entry and command gates, caller identity, actual
poll branch and adapter return. Attribute direct accessor completion to
one caller-owned read context. Pass no context to the queued HIF worker:
its completions remain unobserved and cannot certify ordinary shutdown.
Count fallback calls independently of the branch finally taken.

Preserve the original short-circuit evaluations, accesses, effects and
returns, including successful returns after skipped or failed shutdown.
Use the existing HIF initialization ordinal without publishing pointers.

This unselected MT6797 native experiment depends on ten pstore patches
and the DMA capture patch. It supplies no controller, recovery owner,
full kernel, candidate or hardware evidence. The synthetic archive identity
does not certify authorship; this patch is not submission-ready.
